---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import Prose from '../../components/Prose.astro';
import { EMAIL, STATS_REPO, REPO } from '../../config';

const title = 'Privacy';
const description =
	'What cadkit.org collects: no cookies, cookieless page counts on content pages when enabled, nothing from the demo, and your drawings never leave your browser.';
---

<PageLayout title={title} description={description} breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Privacy' }]} eyebrow="Legal">
	<div class="ck-container">
		<Prose>
			<p>
				cadkit.org is a static website for an open-source project. It has no accounts, no forms, no advertising and
				no cookies. This page lists everything that does happen when you visit.
			</p>

			<h2 id="cookies">No cookies</h2>
			<p>
				The site sets no cookies. Two preferences are kept in your browser's local storage and never sent anywhere:
				the colour theme you pick (light or dark) and the programming language you last chose in code examples.
				In the documentation, the sidebar also keeps its open sections and scroll position in session storage, which
				lasts only as long as the browser tab. Clearing site data in your browser removes all of it.
			</p>

			<h2 id="analytics">Page view counts</h2>
			<p>
				When enabled, content pages load Cloudflare Web Analytics, a cookieless page-view counter. It reports
				aggregate figures such as page views, referring sites, countries, browsers, device types and page load
				times; Cloudflare states that it uses no cookies, no local storage and no fingerprinting. It is not loaded
				on the demo pages or on the “page not found” page, and the site uses no other analytics or tracking.
			</p>

			<h2 id="demo">The demo</h2>
			<p>
				The <a href="/demo/">demo</a> opens drawings in your browser with cadkit compiled to WebAssembly. Files you
				open are read and rendered locally and are never uploaded. The demo pages load no analytics, and their
				content security policy only allows connections back to cadkit.org itself, to fetch the viewer and the
				sample files.
			</p>

			<h2 id="hosting">Hosting</h2>
			<p>
				The site is served by Cloudflare Pages. Like any web host, Cloudflare processes request data (such as IP
				address, requested URL and user agent) to deliver pages and protect the service, and may keep standard
				request logs under its own privacy policy.
			</p>
			<p>
				Fonts, scripts and images are served from cadkit.org; pages make no requests to other sites except the
				optional analytics script above. Links to GitHub, crates.io, PyPI, npm and docs.rs take you to those
				services, whose own policies apply.
			</p>

			<h2 id="stats">Project statistics</h2>
			<p>
				The <a href="/stats/">statistics page</a> shows only aggregate public counts published by crates.io, PyPI,
				npm and GitHub, collected by the open <a href={STATS_REPO}>cadkit-stats</a> repository. It contains no data
				about individual people, and it is built ahead of time, so viewing it contacts no other service.
			</p>

			<h2 id="libraries">The cadkit libraries</h2>
			<p>
				cadkit itself, the libraries, bindings and command-line tool, contains no telemetry and no network code. It
				never reports anything about you or your drawings. The source is public: <a href={REPO}>{REPO.replace('https://', '')}</a>.
			</p>

			<h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
			<p>
				Questions about this page: <a href={`mailto:${EMAIL.hello}`}>{EMAIL.hello}</a>.
			</p>
		</Prose>
	</div>
</PageLayout>
